---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="TypeScript API reference"
   summary="Import screen reader sessions, axe scans, WCAG data, page inspection, and host diagnostics from the a11ied package."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section>
      <h2>Install</h2>
      <pre><code>npm install a11ied</code></pre>
      <p>Import public functions from <code>a11ied</code>. Install the package globally instead if you need the <code>a1</code> command in your shell.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Screen reader API</p>
         <h2>Start and drive a session</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'}
  runDriverSessionAction,
  startDriverSession,
  stopDriverSession,
{'}'} from 'a11ied';

const session = await startDriverSession('virtual');

try {'{'}
  const result = await runDriverSessionAction(session.sessionId, 'next');
  console.log(result.state.lastSpokenPhrase);
{'}'} finally {'{'}
  await stopDriverSession(session.sessionId);
{'}'}</code></pre>
      <p>Pass <code>voiceover</code>, <code>nvda</code>, <code>virtual</code>, or <code>undefined</code> to <code>startDriverSession</code>. An undefined target chooses the available platform default.</p>
      <p>Use <code>getDriverSessionStatus</code> to read state without moving the cursor. Use <code>runEphemeralDriverAction</code> when you do not need a persistent session or transcript.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Axe API</p>
         <h2>Scan a URL</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} runAxe {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const result = await runAxe('http://localhost:3000/checkout', {'{'}
  url: 'http://localhost:3000/checkout',
  wcagVersion: '2.2',
  level: 'AA',
{'}'});

console.log(result.violations);</code></pre>
      <p>Select a scan with <code>level</code>, <code>criterion</code>, or <code>ruleIds</code>. Omit all three to run every axe rule mapped in the selected WCAG version.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">WCAG API</p>
         <h2>Look up criteria and coverage</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} showWcagCoverage, showWcagCriterion {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const criterion = showWcagCriterion('1.1.1', '2.2');
const coverage = showWcagCoverage('1.1.1', '2.2');</code></pre>
      <p><code>listWcagLevels</code> and <code>listWcagCriteria</code> browse the bundled data. <code>searchWcagCriteria</code> returns ranked keyword matches.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Inspect API</p>
         <h2>Check what applies to a page</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} inspectApplicableUrl, inspectCriterionUrl {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const matrix = await inspectApplicableUrl('http://localhost:3000', '2.2');
const labels = await inspectCriterionUrl('1.3.1', 'http://localhost:3000', '2.2');</code></pre>
      <p>Use the <code>Target</code> variants when the input is HTML, a Storybook story, or another resolved document target rather than a live URL.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Host diagnostics</p>
         <h2>Check available targets</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>import {'{'} createDoctorReport, listSupportedTargets {'}'} from 'a11ied';

const report = createDoctorReport();
const targets = listSupportedTargets();</code></pre>
      <p><code>resolveAvailableDefaultTarget</code> selects the real screen reader available on the host and falls back to the virtual target.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Export map</p>
      <h2>Exported helper groups</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Driver sessions</strong><span><code>startDriverSession</code>, <code>getDriverSessionStatus</code>, <code>runDriverSessionAction</code>, <code>runEphemeralDriverAction</code>, <code>stopDriverSession</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Driver commands</strong><span><code>listDriverCommands</code>, <code>resolveDriverCommand</code>, <code>driverCommandSets</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Axe</strong><span><code>runAxe</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>WCAG</strong><span><code>listWcagLevels</code>, <code>listWcagCriteria</code>, <code>showWcagCriterion</code>, <code>searchWcagCriteria</code>, <code>showWcagCoverage</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Inspect</strong><span><code>inspectApplicableTarget</code>, <code>inspectApplicableUrl</code>, <code>inspectCriterionTarget</code>, <code>inspectCriterionUrl</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Browser targets</strong><span><code>resolveDocumentTarget</code>, <code>openUrlInSystemAutomationBrowser</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Diagnostics</strong><span><code>createDoctorReport</code>, <code>renderDoctorText</code>, <code>listSupportedTargets</code>, <code>resolveAvailableDefaultTarget</code></span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         The package also exports driver option and result types. Read the generated TypeScript
         declarations for the complete type surface.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2>Packages</h2>
      <p>The repository divides the runtime into these packages:</p>
      <ul>
         <li><code>@a11ied/contracts</code>: shared runtime schemas and result shapes</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/core</code>: WCAG lookup, target resolution, driver orchestration, axe scans, and doctor reports</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/guidepup</code>: platform adapters for VoiceOver, NVDA, and the virtual reader</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/wcag-data</code>: standards-data sync and normalization</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/wcag-engine</code>: lookup, search, coverage, and applicability over generated artifacts</li>
         <li><code>@a11ied/mcp-server</code>: MCP server entrypoint</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The <code>a11ied</code> package re-exports the public core helpers. Use a scoped package only when you need its lower-level surface.</p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Stable imports</p>
         <h2>Import from the package entrypoint</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         Import from the <code>a11ied</code> entrypoint. Internal file paths inside the package
         may change between releases.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
